# A Spinloop whose values reference environment variables, so one committed
# file works on every machine. `$FOO`, `${FOO}` and `${FOO:-default}` work in
# every value — typed instructions, PARAM values and preset entry values —
# resolved when a command consumes them (`serve`, `cloud deploy`, `apply`) —
# parsing and exporting keep the raw text. See README.md.
PROVIDER llamacpp
ALIAS    qwen3.8-27b
CONTEXT  ${CTX:-32768}    # match the server's --ctx-size, or set CTX per box
PRESET   ./preset.ini     # values resolve as the preset is read; keys don't
PARAM    ngl = ${NGL:-99} # offload every layer unless NGL says otherwise
# ENV QUANT=UD-Q5_K_XL    # uncomment: deploy and a node wake apply the Spinloop's
                          # own ENV lines before they build, so an ENV line can
                          # supply what any reference expands to
